> In the lecture, I am showing the difference between setting the latent variable to have a variance of 1, vs. setting a path. In the lecture, I show that it doesn't make a different for the z-scores of the relationships between the latent variables. But, when I do this in lavaan using std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE rather than std.lv <http://std.lv>= FALSE, I get quite different results. Some paths go from being significant to not, etc.
