> > I run several multiple regressions with lavaan, where some models are
> > nested by putting constraints on the paths. I need the intercepts, so I
> > set meanstructure to TRUE. Now I am not sure about the fixed.x option. I
> > read the help page for it, but I am not sure what would be the correct
> > way of doing it.
> >
> > When no constraints are present, results are identical (fixed.x = TRUE
> > or FALSE), but as soon as one path is constrained to be 0, or other
> > equality constraints are set, results can diverge a lot.

> > If the results diverge, is is most likely a bug. But the dev version has fixed many issues in this area (the special case of univariate regression). Could you try again with dev version?
> >
> > fixed.x=TRUE or FALSE should have NO effect on the final parameter estimates.

With the dev version parameter estimates still diverge in some cases, as soon as a parameter constraint is present (see example below).
Interestingly, s3a, s3b, and s2b give identical results; model s2a throws an error and has different parameter estimates:

